/-! # Full-support bounded coherent complexes generate the ring

Source: the agent full-support generation corollary in the DAG, using Stacks Project,
Algebra, Tags 00L0 and 00L4, Derived Categories, Tags 09SJ and 0149, and More on Algebra,
Tag 09PB. These tags provide ingredients, rather than stating this corollary verbatim.
(blueprint: lem-sfb-noetherian-full-support-localizing-generation).
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u w

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits CategoryTheory.MonoidalCategory

namespace DerivedCategory

/-- A bounded complex with finite cohomology and full prime-local support over a commutative
Noetherian ring generates the degree-zero ring under isomorphisms, shifts, distinguished
triangles, retracts, and coproducts indexed in the module universe. Membership in the smallest
such full subcategory is expressed by membership in every such object property containing `E`.
The tensor is the published K-flat derived monoidal tensor; the localization is regarded as a
`B`-module, so its tensor with `E` is the underlying `B`-object of the localized complex.
There is no assumption of finite projective or injective dimension, or of a nonzero ring.

Source: the agent corollary using Stacks Project, Tags 00L0 (`lemma-filter-Noetherian-module`),
00L4 (`lemma-filter-primes-in-support`), 09SJ (`definition-generators`),
0149 (`lemma-representable-homological`), and 09PB (`remark-P-resolution`).
(blueprint: lem-sfb-noetherian-full-support-localizing-generation).

Proof plan (the seven steps of the DAG node):
1. If `B = 0`, its degree-zero object is zero and belongs to the subcategory as the empty
   coproduct. Otherwise let `L` be the localizing subcategory generated by `E`.
2. For `X` in `L`, the objects `N` for which `X ⊗ N` belongs to `L` form a localizing
   subcategory: derived tensor is exact (lem-pc-derived-tensor-second-factor-functor) and
   preserves coproducts, computed by direct sums of K-flat complexes
   (def-pc-module-kflat-complex, lem-pc-derived-module-direct-sums). This subcategory contains
   `B[0]`, hence is all of `D(B)` by lem-pc-derived-module-free-generation. Thus `L` is a
   tensor ideal, and contains `E ⊗ κ(p)` for every prime `p`.
3. Localize at `p`. The localization is a Noetherian local ring; exact flat localization
   preserves bounded finite cohomology (lem-weil-pbc-localization-module-exact,
   lem-weil-pbc-localization-flat). The hypothesis makes the localized `E` nonzero.
   Apply lem-trf-local-derived-tensor-nonvanishing with the residue field, and use
   lem-pc-derived-tensor-transitivity to obtain `E ⊗ κ(p) ≠ 0`.
4. By lem-trf-field-complex-cohomology-splitting this residue-field complex splits into
   its cohomology without any boundedness assumption. A nonzero cohomology vector supplies
   a line retract; restricting scalars, then using retract and shift closure, puts `κ(p)[0]`
   in `L` for every prime `p`.
5. If some `(B/J)[0]` is absent, choose a maximal counterexample ideal using Noetherianity.
   A prime filtration (lem-weil-pbc-noetherian-module-prime-filtration) and its short exact
   sequence triangles (lem-weil-pbc-complex-ses-triangle) show that this ideal must be prime:
   otherwise all filtration primes strictly contain it and maximality puts every factor in `L`.
6. For this prime `p`, put `C = κ(p)/(B/p)`. Every finite submodule of `C` is killed by `p`
   and by some element outside `p`, by multiplying denominators. Its prime filtration
   therefore has factors `B/q` with `q` strictly larger than `p`, hence in `L`. Filtration
   triangles put the submodule in `L`. The finite submodules form a small nonempty directed
   poset with union `C`; lem-sfb-module-localizing-filtered-colimits puts `C[0]` in `L`.
7. The exact sequence `0 → B/p → κ(p) → C → 0` and its triangle
   (lem-weil-pbc-complex-ses-triangle), rotated, put `(B/p)[0]` in `L`, a contradiction.
   Thus every quotient belongs to `L`; take `J = 0` to obtain `B[0]`. -/
theorem noetherian_full_support_localizing_generation
    (B : Type u) [CommRing B] [IsNoetherianRing B]
    [HasDerivedCategory.{w} (ModuleCat.{u} B)]
    (E : DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} B))
    (hbounded : ∃ a b : ℤ, a ≤ b ∧ ∀ j : ℤ, j < a ∨ b < j →
      IsZero ((homologyFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} B) j).obj E))
    (hfinite : ∀ j : ℤ, Module.Finite B ((homologyFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} B) j).obj E))
    (hsupport : ∀ (p : Ideal B) [p.IsPrime],
      ¬ IsZero (E ⊗ (singleFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} B) 0).obj
        (ModuleCat.of B (Localization.AtPrime p))))
    (P : ObjectProperty (DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} B)))
    [P.IsClosedUnderIsomorphisms] [P.IsTriangulated] [P.IsStableUnderRetracts]
    [∀ I : Type u, P.IsClosedUnderColimitsOfShape (Discrete I)]
    (hE : P E) :
    P ((singleFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} B) 0).obj (ModuleCat.of B B)) := by
  sorry

end DerivedCategory
